// Unattached-candidate alert: raise for review when a release candidate has
// been sitting without its source attachment for longer than the host's
// grace period. HAS_RELEASE_CANDIDATE is 1 once a draft release note exists;
// HAS_SOURCE_ATTACHMENT is 1 once that draft carries the merge, commit or
// artifact it is describing; PENDING_AGE_SECONDS is how long the candidate has
// been in that state, in whole seconds.
// The age term is the whole rule. A candidate with no attachment is normal for
// the first few minutes of writing it; a candidate with no attachment an hour
// later is a note nobody can check against anything.
// REGIME: all of them. This is a property of the draft, not of the system it
// describes.
// CONDITIONS: the host resets PENDING_AGE_SECONDS when the candidate is
// revised, so the age measures the current state rather than the candidate's
// whole life.
// INVALIDATION: the attachment arriving, or the candidate being withdrawn.
// Either takes the rule out of its trigger with no memory of having fired.
// SHAPE: 5m against an hour-long threshold, so the alert lands within a
// twelfth of the grace period it is measuring.
// NOT aether_release_notes_uncovered_merge: that one fires when no candidate
// exists at all. This one fires when a candidate exists and cannot be traced
// back to what it claims to describe.
// CALIBRATED ON: a one-hour grace period, which is a policy figure and does
// not travel - a programme that drafts notes in a batch at the end of the week
// should raise it, and one that generates them automatically should lower it
// until the threshold is longer than the generator's own latency.
strategy AetherReleaseNotesCandidateUnattached {

    agent ReleaseDesk

    every 5m {

        if HAS_RELEASE_CANDIDATE >= 1 and HAS_SOURCE_ATTACHMENT <= 0 and PENDING_AGE_SECONDS >= 3600 {

            observe()

        }

    }

}
